quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  11,54,"All we can say is that some of our gods may have inflicted some harm on you.’ He said: ‘I call Allah to witness, and you too be (my) witness, that I disown what you ascribe as partners,"
  11,55,"besides Him. So scheme against me all together, then do not grant me any respite."
  11,56,"I have put my trust in Allah—my Lord and your Lord. No moving creature is on the earth, but He holds it by its forelock. Indeed, (the way of) my Lord is (to be) on the straight path (of truth and justice)."
  11,57,"But if you turn away, I have already conveyed to you the message with which I was sent to you. And my Lord will cause other people to succeed you, and you cannot harm Him in the least. Indeed, my Lord is Watcher over everything.’"
  11,58,"And when Our command came, We saved Hud and those who believed along with him by a mercy from Us. And We saved them from harsh punishment."
  11,59,"Such were the (people of) ‘Ad: they denied the signs of their Lord, disobeyed His messengers and followed the command of every tyrant opposer of truth."
  11,60,"They were pursued by a curse in this world as on the Day of Resurrection. Yes! The ‘Ad surely denied their Lord. So away with the ‘Ad, the people of Hud!"
  11,61,"And to (the people of) Thamud, (We sent) their (fellow) brother Salih. He said: ‘O my people! Worship Allah. You have no god other than Him. He brought you into being from the earth and settled you in it. So, seek forgiveness from Him and turn to Him in repentance. My Lord is indeed Ever Near, All-Responsive.’"
  11,62,"They said: ‘O Salih! You were a source of hope among us before this. Do you (now) forbid us to worship what our fathers have been worshipping? Indeed, we are in grave doubt about what you are calling us to.’"
